#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:5
#: 01902ac5176c4658a9c9334413d801a7
msgid "Gimbal / Mount Controls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:6
#: 4099d661c3d74f499503185ae917ce14
msgid "ArduPilot provides mechanisms to control the pointing direction (aka targeting) automatically for camera mounts (know hereafter as ``mounts``), as well as by pilot commands/controls. Mounts can be commanded point in at least six different ways (``targeting modes``) by ArduPilot.  This page provides an overview of these controls and their setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:8
#: cd650d86db6d406a99b889ad6429c944
msgid "ArduPilot supports up to two mounts. Each mount has parameters associated with it, e.g.  :ref:`MNT1_TYPE<MNT1_TYPE>`, :ref:`MNT2_TYPE<MNT2_TYPE>`, :ref:`MNT1_RC_RATE<MNT1_RC_RATE>`, :ref:`MNT2_RC_RATE<MNT2_RC_RATE>`, etc. For the remainder of the article, we will use MNT1 for examples of setups and parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:10
#: 796a5c62d49447508a084ccaca09cd1a
msgid "The mount's \"targeting mode\" defines how it is controlled.  Each ground station (GCS) is different but Mission Planner, for example, has a \"Set Mount\" button that allows changing the mode.  In many cases the user does not need to directly set the mode, instead this is done automatically as part of responding to a command from the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:16
#: 845c83d5822c43ce9a9965aafe1cdc98
msgid "In order to enable the mount, a :ref:`MNT1_TYPE<MNT1_TYPE>` must be selected corresponding to the mount type. This will allow its mount parameters to be seen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:19
#: 6ec95f9be1ab4840bd0408bc37cbb9e1
msgid "Targeting Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:20
#: d981b60d85f54aeaa5038c2c5d9a2c15
msgid "Below are the 6 supported targeting modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:22
#: e0eef1b19d7b43158652216fda57a9e4
msgid "**Retract Mode:** the mount will move to the roll, pitch and yaw angles held in the :ref:`MNT1_RETRACT_X<MNT1_RETRACT_X>`, :ref:`MNT1_RETRACT_Y<MNT1_RETRACT_Y>`, :ref:`MNT1_RETRACT_Z<MNT1_RETRACT_Z>` parameters respectively.  Some special mount specific behaviours:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:24
#: e9b7f593f0e946758897f74c41675d28
msgid ":ref:`Gremsy mounts <common-gremsy-pixyu-gimbal>` will immediately stop stabilising"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:25
#: cc87dd95daef40019135a01cefd92390
msgid ":ref:`Servo mount <common-camera-gimbal>` will move to the specified angles and stop stabilising."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:26
#: 2e1fede7a04243d8bab28992807afd22
msgid ":ref:`Siyi mounts <common-siyi-zr10-gimbal>` do not provide roll control so the roll angle (:ref:`MNT1_RETRACT_X<MNT1_RETRACT_X>`) is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:28
#: 758701fec5394ca79c16e949ce66cd7a
msgid "If a servo has been setup to mechanically deploy/retract the mount (``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` = 9 for MNT1, \"15\" for MNT2) it will be commanded to retract the mount. Changing to another mode will command the servo to deploy the mount."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:30
#: 8dbc73ada6cf447fbd538c666b0e6e74
msgid "**Neutral Mode:** the mount will move to the roll, pitch and yaw angles held in the :ref:`MNT1_NEUTRAL_X<MNT1_NEUTRAL_X>`, :ref:`MNT1_NEUTRAL_Y<MNT1_NEUTRAL_Y>`, :ref:`MNT1_NEUTRAL_Z<MNT1_NEUTRAL_Z>`, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:32
#: 0e2915f050a04d6d903d2abf10df4565
msgid "**MAVLink Targeting:** the mount will move according to real-time commands received from the ground stations, companion computers or other MAVLink command source, and/or Auto mode mission commands. See :ref:`mav_cmd_do_gimbal_manager_pitchyaw`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:34
#: 57f637f3b36646e6a9e4523e9533b117
msgid "**RC Targeting:** the pilot controls the mount in real-time using the RC transmitter. See section below for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:36
#: 41b32fb1683947f29768a3f5e61ab243
msgid "**GPS Point:** same as MAVLink targeting but ArduPilot forces the mount to point at a specific location.  Users never need to actively set the mount to this mode. The user usually selects a point and altitude on the GCS map and selects a right click menu item to \"Point the camera here\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:38
#: 3b46c184db824d529b32524742ef6648
msgid "**SysId Target:** the mount points at another vehicle with the MAVLink system id specified.  Users never need to actively set the mount to this mode and there are no known GCSs that support setting the system id, but the parameter can be set by updating the value of :ref:`MNT1_SYSID_DFLT<MNT1_SYSID_DFLT>` directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:40
#: cbdabcb62abd49f1ab60eccd770a6021
msgid "**Home Location:** the mount points at Home (normally its location when armed, unless changed by the user in the GCS)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:42
#: c608f86a15d04ec7a08f63908d4e99ad
msgid "The mount's default mode on startup can be set with the :ref:`MNT1_DEFLT_MODE<MNT1_DEFLT_MODE>` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:44
#: 56f38bfa00b44c2eae3312550b693d1a
msgid "ArduPilot 4.5 (and higher) automatically switches the mount to RC Targeting Mode if the pilot moves any configured Roll/Pitch/Yaw RC targeting inputs (see below) by the larger of 10uS or ``RCx_DZ``.  The only exception is if the mounts is in RETRACT mode in which case the mount mode will not be automatically changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:47
#: 60a0104de2ef4f22b3d473174aa1865a
msgid "Mount Internal Axis Locks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:48
#: e0149fb73e294471849b5d539d5baa9d
msgid "The above modes concern how pitch, roll, and yaw axis *TARGETs* are sent to the mount. But many mounts have internal controls for how those targets for pitch, roll, and yaw are interpreted. Those positioning commands can be interpreted by the mount as being with respect to Earth frame reference or Body frame. Body frame are angle targets on each axis measured with respect to the mount itself, while Earth frame is interpreted to be with respect the horizon and compass heading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:50
#: 27740388039440ed98a3253026b95f5f
msgid "For example, at 30 deg negative pitch target would be 30 deg down from the mount's zero point with respect to its mounting in Body frame, but 30 deg below the earth's horizon in Earth frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:52
#: a7bbe804cef743ec881596d1eac6d15c
msgid "Most mounts have internal controls for each axis to determine how to interpret the targets. ArduPilot sets the mount's pitch and roll axis frame (if configurable) to Earth frame interpretations for all Mount types via its driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:54
#: b59fa86de0b849ab856fd8ab5d25a1bd
msgid "The yaw axis is forced to Earth frame for the GPS Point, Home, and SysID modes, and is otherwise body frame controlled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:57
#: 46a1dbbe72764995b032285a1278c078
msgid "Mount RC failsafe position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:58
#: f9d02ff22a3a4369a4f242e02832e50a
msgid "In the event of an RC failsafe, the mount can be moved to the Neutral mode position if the ``MNTx_OPTIONS`` bit 1 is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:61
#: 329d6eb026434fb6a6e38e3cdf143fd0
msgid "Control with an RC transmitter (aka RC Targeting)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:62
#: 7904d3b8797f411e985b013860773728
msgid "While the mount is in \"RC Targeting\" mode (see above for how to change modes), the pilot can control the mount's target roll, pitch and yaw angles using an RC transmitter channel for each axis. For example (RC channels shown are for example only, and can be any channel not otherwise used):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:64
#: 01ed44757bb24ca8bd8c14a15200ef54
msgid "set :ref:`RC6_OPTION <RC6_OPTION>` = 212 (\"Mount1 Roll\") to control the mount's roll angle with RC channel 6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:65
#: e7132b0347bb4f63814e9565ab646597
msgid "set :ref:`RC7_OPTION <RC7_OPTION>` = 213 (\"Mount1 Pitch\") to control the mount's pitch angle with RC channel 7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:66
#: f8ae5702e71d4c17b33a51261b5bf477
msgid "set :ref:`RC8_OPTION <RC8_OPTION>` = 214 (\"Mount1 Yaw\") to control the mount's yaw angle with RC channel 8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:67
#: f9fadee3879d403ba0c550e8c37a099f
msgid "ensure the RCx_TRIM parameter for each RC input channel used is half way between RCx_MIN and RCx_MAX"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:69
#: 736207ebe1fe4e07b5b1aed0e3b60caf
msgid "By default the RC input specifies the **angle** but this can be changed to **rate** control by setting :ref:`MNT1_RC_RATE <MNT1_RC_RATE>` to a **non-zero** desired rotation rate in deg/sec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:71
#: dc3d8d7f6cf24afe891bb32f4bd89516
msgid "The pilot can retract the mount with the \"Retract Mount1\" or \"Retract Mount2\" auxiliary switch (using RC 10 in the below example.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:73
#: 3bab02d690954c44a18eded324663dc7
msgid ":ref:`RC10_OPTION <RC10_OPTION>` = 27 (\"Retract Mount1\") to change the mount to Retract mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:74
#: e1545ca55e704f6c9e079fb8881612e4
msgid ":ref:`RC10_OPTION <RC10_OPTION>` = 113 (\"Retract Mount2\") to change the mount to Retract mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:77
#: b472cb8a289a4980b0871c68cffb6e9d
msgid "Axis Lock Auxiliary Switches and Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mount-targeting.rst:79
#: 5d13305f73d9476d9eca7b64f89963ba
msgid "If the mount is capable, the roll and pitch axes can be controlled in the RC Targeting mode with an auxiliary switch on an RC channel, if you use ANGLE, not RATE controls (eg. :ref:`MNT1_RC_RATE <MNT1_RC_RATE>` = 0. In the future this will be expanded to RATE control also). For example using RC channel 9, set :ref:`RC9_OPTION <RC9_OPTION>` = 185 to enable this switch. Switching its position will force roll and/or pitch angles of the mount to be stabilized ('locked\") in earth frame (ie with respect to the horizon) or body frame (with respect to the gimbals base)"
msgstr ""

